# Casa del Trueque de la Ruta 18 (Route 18's trade house: a creature for a creature, C9, contract 56), 9 x 7, interior. column = i, row = j. A tinkerer's room: the trader at the back, a table, books, crates.
# He wants a SAGATEE and gives a TONGUARD (a creature) whose nickname is the fixed ASCII text `tr18.nick` (Marc, the same in all four languages: the trade idiom of casa_trueque). Flag 914 = the trade was done.
@map casa_lengua
@size 9 7
@interior yes
@bg 3
@fill floor_wood
@spawn door 4 5 N
@flag tonguard_done 914
@var tg_res 5
@var tg_want 6
@var tg_give 7
@legend
  .  tile=floor_wood
  C  tile=none object=wall_corner
  w  tile=none object=wall_j
  y  tile=none object=wall_win_j
  |  tile=none object=wall_i
  B  object=bookshelf interact=look text=tr18.books
  H  object=crate_plain
  x  object=barrel
  T  object=table
  L  npc=trueque id=trader face=SW script=trader
  m  tile=mat
@grid
  Cwwywwyww
  |B.....H.
  |...L....
  |.x...T..
  |.x......
  |........
  |...mm...
@warp m -> ruta_18 spawn=lengua_door
@script trader npc
    npc_face_hero trader
    setv tg_want sp:sagatee
    setv tg_give sp:tonguard
    name_var 0 tg_want
    name_var 1 tg_give
    jf tonguard_done after
    say tr18.hello
    ask tr18.ask
    jv 0 1 go
    say tr18.no
    end
  go:
    trade sagatee tonguard tr18.nick tg_res
    jv tg_res 1 done
    jv tg_res 255 cancel
    say tr18.wrong
    end
  cancel:
    say tr18.no
    end
  done:
    setf tonguard_done
    say tr18.done
    end
  after:
    name_var 0 tg_give
    say tr18.after
@end
